3c:["$","p","p-5",{"children":"The Haramain high-speed railway is faster between stations, and a good option for a light-travelling adult. But:"}]
3d:["$","ul","ul-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Madinah station is not at the Haram"}]," — you need a car to get there, with your luggage."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Makkah station is not beside the Haram either"}]," — you need a second car to your hotel."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":["You must be in Ihram ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"before"}]," the train passes the Miqat, so you change at the hotel or stop at Abyar Ali on the way to the station."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Trains have luggage limits and set departure times."}],"\n"]}]
3e:["$","p","p-6",{"children":["For a family with luggage, those two extra transfers often cancel out the time saved. For a solo traveller with a small bag, the train is a fine choice. The ",["$","$L26","a-0",{"href":"/guides/makkah-to-madinah-transport-guide","children":"Makkah–Madinah comparison guide"}]," has more detail."]}]
3f:["$","h2","h2-5",{"id":"how-the-fare-works","children":"How the fare works"}]
40:["$","p","p-7",{"children":["The fare covers the whole journey from your Madinah pickup to your Makkah drop-off, including the Miqat stop and a rest stop if you mention them when booking. It depends on the vehicle class and any extra stops — ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"not"}]," on the time of day or demand. Pay ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"cash to the driver or by bank transfer"}],"; an ",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"electronic receipt"}]," is available on request. ",["$","strong","strong-3",{"children":"Free cancellation up to 24 hours before pickup."}]]}]
41:["$","h2","h2-6",{"id":"common-questions","children":"Common questions"}]
42:["$","h3","h3-0",{"id":"how-long-is-the-drive-from-madinah-to-makkah","children":"How long is the drive from Madinah to Makkah?"}]
43:["$","p","p-8",{"children":"About 4 hours for roughly 430 km in normal traffic, plus time at the Miqat and any rest stop."}]
44:["$","h3","h3-1",{"id":"can-we-stop-at-abyar-ali-for-ihram","children":"Can we stop at Abyar Ali for Ihram?"}]
45:["$","p","p-9",{"children":"Yes — tell us when you book and the stop is part of the trip."}]
46:["$","h3","h3-2",{"id":"can-we-leave-late-at-night","children":"Can we leave late at night?"}]
47:["$","p","p-10",{"children":"Yes. Bookings are available 24/7, and many families travel overnight in summer."}]
48:["$","h3","h3-3",{"id":"is-there-anything-to-see-on-the-way","children":"Is there anything to see on the way?"}]
49:["$","p","p-11",{"children":["The drive is mostly open desert and rocky hills, so most families just make the Miqat and rest stops. If you want to visit the historic site of Badr, book a separate ",["$","$L26","a-0",{"href":"/services/badr-ziyarat","children":"Badr Ziyarat"}]," from Madinah — it is not on the direct highway."]}]
